  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Description"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "In the Work In Progress report the Inv. Hrs column shows two decimal places \u2014 for example +0.50, +1.24, -0.81, -14.86, and a zero reads 0.00. The Totals row does the same. One decimal place is asked for."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Steps to reproduce"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Environment: QA branch sv8582 (https://sv8582.qa.shopview.com), build v3.5-f77875c. Desktop browser, signed in as an Admin."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "orderedList",
     "attrs": {
      "order": 1
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Open Reports, then Work In Progress, and set the date range to Last 12 Months, with both locations, Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 and Staging Lethbridge - 4310 selected."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Open Column Selection and switch Inv. Hrs on."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Read any value in that column, and the Totals row at the bottom. This was checked on all four tabs."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Current behaviour"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Every value carries two decimal places \u2014 +0.50, +1.24, -0.81, -14.86 \u2014 and a zero reads 0.00. The Totals row does the same: +246.84, +1434.65, +0.52, +173.50."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The sign is right, the zero is correctly unsigned, the arithmetic is right and the green and red colouring is correct. It is the number of decimal places only."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Expected behaviour"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Inv. Hrs shows a signed number with one decimal place \u2014 the same values would read +0.5, +1.2, -0.8, -14.9 \u2014 and a zero reads 0.0, unsigned."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rule"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Source",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " \u2014 "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "the "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Work In Progress report specification",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "link",
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://shopview.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020aa00b8d6a71f4259891982a304227c20/pages/703660034/WIP+Work+In+Progress+Report"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " on Confluence, version 9, requirement S4-R23: \u201cInv. Hrs shows the quoted labor hours minus the worked (clocked) labor hours across the approved lines, as a signed number with one decimal place (\"+2.0\", \"-14.0\", \"0.0\"). A zero value shows unsigned as \"0.0\" (never \"+0.0\" or blank).\u201d"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
